# Window: command log replay during whole-cluster recovery.
#   CommandLogReinitiatorImpl$TaskMessageConsumer.run reinitiates each logged
#   transaction through TransactionCreator.createTransaction.
#
# Fault: delay each of the first 50 transactions a host reinitiates by
#   100 ms, so its replay runs about 5 s longer. Each partition's log is
#   replayed by one host (CommandLogReplayState.shouldSkip), so the rule is
#   in every node's startup script and only the replaying hosts (usually
#   one) are delayed. Loaded at startup, since replay starts before a rule
#   could be submitted.
#
# Correct behaviour: recovery completes with every acknowledged
#   transaction present (the workload checker); it never skips records.

RULE replay-delay
CLASS org.voltdb.CommandLogReinitiatorImpl$TaskMessageConsumer
METHOD run
AT INVOKE createTransaction
IF incrementCounter("replay-delay") <= 50
DO traceln("BYTEMAN replay-delay fired");
   delay(100)
ENDRULE
